  "dispositionsRecorded": "2026-09-04",
  "decisions": {
    "paths": "Skills must not hardcode vendor paths. Declared in AGENTS.md when the repo declares one; otherwise a fixed documented default. Discovery/heuristic scanning rejected: nondeterministic across sessions.",
    "docs-superpowers-rename": "Executed 2026-09-04: docs/superpowers/{specs,plans} -> docs/{designs,plans}; 34 citations across 15 files. Two references intentionally left in docs/reviews/2026-07-05-telemetry-plan/ where a reviewer quotes the old path while arguing against it.",
    "installer-destructive": "Measured 2026-09-04: `skills experimental_install` rm -rf's each skill dir and copies from unpinned upstream HEAD. skills:setup guard changed from completeness-count to existence so the destructive path is unreachable once a tree exists.",
    "retired": "find-skills (vercel registry surface, zero inbound refs) and using-superpowers (Skill-tool bootstrap; premise fails in an auto-injecting harness). tdd folded into test-driven-development, which keeps the name 7 cross-references point at.",
    "namespace": "superpowers:<name> prefixes stripped to bare names. A stale vendor prefix resolves to no skill silently.",
    "structure": "Companion files grouped by role: references/ (docs an agent reads), prompts/ (subagent templates), scripts/ (executables), examples/. Previously four skills held 3-6 files flat in the skill root.",
    "cross-skill": "Skills never assume another skill is installed. Frontmatter `uses:` declares name + source (github repo) so a harness can resolve or fetch; body text degrades to a manual fallback when the skill is absent.",
    "provenance-paths": "Local companion regrouping (references/, prompts/, scripts/) changed paths that upstream still holds flat. Each file records upstreamPath when the local path differs, so status is recomputed against snapshot bytes rather than assumed from the local name.",
